Article 3 (Composition)
(1) The Committee shall consist of not more than 20 members, including one Chairperson. <Amended on April 27, 2015; March 22, 2021>
(2) The Deputy Secretary General of the Constitutional Court shall serve as Chairperson, and members shall be commissioned or appointed by the Secretary General of the Constitutional Court from among persons falling under any of the following subparagraphs: <Amended on April 27, 2015; March 22, 2021>
1. Constitutional researchers, assistant constitutional researchers, or constitutional research officers;
2. General-service public officials of Grade IV or higher of the Constitutional Court;
3. Persons serving as assistant professors or higher in law or information-technology-related fields at accredited universities;
4. Experts in fields of work necessary for promoting informatization of the Constitutional Court.
(3) The term of office of a commissioned member shall be two years and may be renewed. <Newly Inserted on April 27, 2015; March 22, 2021>
(4) The Committee shall have two secretaries for smooth operation; the heads of the Informatization Planning Division and the Information Security Division of the Secretariat of the Constitutional Court shall serve as secretaries. <Newly Inserted on March 22, 2021>
(5) Where a member is deemed unable to perform his or her duties due to an unavoidable reason, the Secretary General of the Constitutional Court may dismiss or remove the member from office. <Amended on April 27, 2015>
